# {{.Name}}

A [Tern](https://github.com/Unfield/Tern) app: Svelte on the client, Go on the server.

## Develop

```sh
npm install
npm run dev        # or: go tool tern dev
```

Open <http://localhost:5173>. Svelte changes update instantly; Go changes rebuild and restart the server.

## Build

```sh
npm run build      # or: go tool tern build
./build/{{.Name}}
```

`tern build` produces a single binary with the client embedded. It listens on `PORT` (default 3000).

## Project layout

```
src/
  app.html              HTML template
  routes/
    +layout.svelte      layout for every page
    +page.svelte        the home page
    page.server.go      its Load function and form actions
    about/+page.svelte  /about
static/                 files served as-is
main.go                 starts the server
```

The Tern CLI is pinned in `go.mod` as a Go tool, so `go tool tern` always matches the version of the `kit` package your code imports. Update both with `go get -tool github.com/Unfield/Tern/cmd/tern@latest`.
